@startuml

start

:Thermal management controller executes as state machine within RTOS;
fork
:Govern PWM fan speeds;
fork again
:Govern liquid-cooling pump duty cycles;
end fork

:User entry;
:Initiate sensor fusion routine;
if (Ambient temperature > preset threshold?) then (yes)
  :Command HVAC system via CAN to reach setpoint;
else (no)
  :Evaluate air quality;
    if (Degraded?) then (yes)
      :Activate purifier;
    else (no)
    end if    
    :Assess ambient light;
    if (Insufficient?) then (yes)
      :Engage lighting;
    else (no)
    end if
end if

:Security check verify door/window status;
if (Open?) then (yes)
  :Dispatch notification;
else (no)
  :Advance to user preference check;
    :Apply custom device profiles/default device profiles;
end if

:Conditional operations managed within preemptively scheduled task model;
fork
  :High-priority ISR handles user instructions from voice/mobile app interfaces;
fork again
  :Medium-priority tasks perform periodic device health checks;
  :Write structured, CRC-protected audit logs to ring buffer;
  :Flush to non-volatile storage under PMIC-managed I/O budget;
end fork

:Dedicated telemetry monitor driven by timer interrupts;
:Run in tight loop;
:Perform sensor data acquisition and calibration;

fork
if (Detect fault?) then (yes)
  :Engage bounded retries with exponential backoff;
else (no)
end if
fork again
if (Critical out-of-range readings?) then (yes)
  :Trigger redundant sensor checks;
  :Initiate controlled system cool-down via FADEC;
else (no)
end if
end fork

:Watchdog timer ensures liveness across all concurrent processes;

stop

@enduml
